  "publishingRemarks": "The MenAfriVac vaccine can be used in a controlled temperature chain (CTC) for up to four days at ambient temperatures not exceeding 40°C.  A CTC is initiated immediately prior to administration provided that the vaccine has not reached its expiry date and the vaccine vial monitor is still valid. Unopened vaccine vials should be discarded at the end of the four days at 40°C. Reconstituted vaccine should be discarded within six hours. WHO recommends that CTC implementation only occur with appropriate planning training and guidance.  For more information please contact vaccines@who.int .",
